## # uuid/core/nanoid
##
## Compact, URL-friendly unique string identifier generator.
## Part of the Alya Language package ecosystem (https://github.com/alya-lang).

import "rand" as rand

## Generates a URL-safe NanoID of the specified size.
##
## ### Parameters
## - `size`: Identifier length. Defaults to `21`.
## - `alphabet`: Sampling alphabet string. Defaults to URL-friendly symbols.
##
## ### Returns
## The generated NanoID string (empty when `size` is not positive).
##
## ### Examples
## ```alya
## let id = core_nanoid(10)
## ```
pub function core_nanoid(size: int = 21, alphabet: string = "_-0123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ") -> string
    if size <= 0
        return ""
    end
    return rand::string(size, alphabet)
end
